<script lang="ts">
  import Backoff from "./Backoff.svelte";

  // A document has one <script>. State for the controls below lives here.
  let attempts = $state(4);
  let base = $state(1);
</script>

# Retries with exponential backoff

## The policy

A client that gets a `503` waits, then tries again. Each wait doubles, so a service that is down for a minute sees a few retries, not a flood. Two numbers set the policy: how many retries, and the first wait.

<div class="controls">
  <label>Retries <input type="range" min="1" max="8" bind:value={attempts} /> <output>{attempts}</output></label>
  <label>First wait (s) <input type="range" min="1" max="5" bind:value={base} /> <output>{base}</output></label>
</div>

<Backoff {attempts} {base} />

The table comes from `Backoff.svelte`, a component next to this document. The two sliders and their state are written inline, in this file.

> [!NOTE]
> Without JavaScript the sliders do not move, and the table shows the prerendered policy: 4 retries from 1 s. Every other part of the page is plain HTML.

## The change

The policy lives in one function, and the client calls it. This git diff touches two files, so it renders as one block with a unified and split switch. The switch needs JavaScript; without it the diff stays unified.

```diff
diff --git a/src/retry.ts b/src/retry.ts
index 3f1a2c4..8d0e9b7 100644
--- a/src/retry.ts
+++ b/src/retry.ts
@@ -1,10 +1,10 @@
-export async function retry<T>(run: () => Promise<T>, attempts = 3): Promise<T> {
+export async function retry<T>(run: () => Promise<T>, attempts = 4, base = 1000): Promise<T> {
   for (let i = 0; ; i++) {
     try {
       return await run();
     } catch (error) {
       if (i >= attempts) throw error;
-      await sleep(1000);
+      await sleep(base * 2 ** i);
     }
   }
 }
diff --git a/src/client.ts b/src/client.ts
index 51b7a0e..c2d4f19 100644
--- a/src/client.ts
+++ b/src/client.ts
@@ -12,2 +12,2 @@ export function getOrder(id: string) {
-  return retry(() => fetchJson(`/orders/${id}`));
+  return retry(() => fetchJson(`/orders/${id}`), 4, 1000);
 }
```

